# 基础词 Unit12
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit12核心词汇

{{confident}}{/ˈkɒnfɪdənt/}{{adj. 自信的；有信心的}}{{She is confident that she will pass the exam.}}
{{confirm}}{/kənˈfɜːrm/}{{v. 确认；证实}}{{The hotel confirmed our reservation by email.}}
{{conflict}}{/ˈkɒnflɪkt/}}n. 冲突；矛盾}}{{The conflict between the two countries lasted for years.}}
{{confront}}{/kənˈfrʌnt/}}v. 面对；对抗}}{{We must confront the problems rather than ignore them.}}
{{confuse}}{/kənˈfjuːz/}}v. 使困惑；混淆}}{{The similar names confused many people.}}
{{congress}}{/ˈkɒŋɡres/}}n. 国会；代表大会}}{{Congress passed the new law after months of debate.}}
{{connect}}{/kəˈnekt/}}v. 连接；联系}}{{The bridge connects the two sides of the river.}}
{{conscious}}{/ˈkɒnʃəs/}}adj. 有意识的；自觉的}}{{She was conscious of the need to work harder.}}
{{consensus}}{/kənˈsensəs/}}n. 共识；一致}}{{The committee reached a consensus on the issue.}}
{{consequence}}{/ˈkɒnsɪkwəns/}}n. 结果；后果}}{{Pollution is a consequence of industrial development.}}
{{conservative}}{/kənˈsɜːrvətɪv/}}adj. 保守的；n. 保守派}}{{He holds conservative views on social issues.}}
{{consider}}{/kənˈsɪdər/}}v. 考虑；认为}}{{Please consider all the options before making a decision.}}
{{consist}}{/kənˈsɪst/}}v. 由…组成；在于}}{{The team consists of twelve members.}}
{{constant}}{/ˈkɒnstənt/}}adj. 不断的；恒定的}}{{The constant noise from the construction site was annoying.}}
{{construct}}{/kənˈstrʌkt/}}v. 建造；构建}}{{They plan to construct a new bridge over the river.}}
{{consult}}{/kənˈsʌlt/}}v. 查阅；咨询}}{{You should consult a doctor about your symptoms.}}
{{consume}}{/kənˈsjuːm/}}v. 消耗；消费；吃}}{{Americans consume a large amount of energy each year.}}
{{contact}}{/ˈkɒntækt/}}n. 接触；联系；v. 联系}}{{Please contact me if you have any questions.}}
{{contain}}{/kənˈteɪn/}}v. 包含；容纳}}{{The box contains all the necessary documents.}}
{{contemporary}}{/kənˈtempərəri/}}adj. 当代的；同时代的}}{{Contemporary art often challenges traditional ideas.}}
{{content}}{/ˈkɒntent/}}n. 内容；满足；adj. 满足的}}{{The content of the book is both informative and有趣.}}
{{contest}}{/ˈkɒntest/}}n. 竞赛；v. 争夺}}{{She won first prize in the speech contest.}}
{{context}}{/ˈkɒntekst/}}n. 上下文；背景}}{{The meaning of a word depends on its context.}}
{{continue}}{/kənˈtɪnjuː/}}v. 继续；持续}}{{The rain continued throughout the night.}}
{{contract}}{/ˈkɒntrækt/}}n. 合同；v. 收缩；感染}}{{Both parties signed the contract yesterday.}}
{{contradict}}{/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt/}}v. 反驳；与…矛盾}}{{The evidence contradicts his earlier statement.}}
{{contribute}}{/kənˈtrɪbjuːt/}}v. 贡献；投稿}}{{Everyone should contribute to the community.}}
{{control}}{/kənˈtrəʊl/}}v./n. 控制；管理}}{{The government is trying to control inflation.}}
{{convince}}{/kənˈvɪns/}}v. 使确信；说服}}{{She convinced me to change my mind about the plan.}}
{{cooperate}}{/kəʊˈɒpəreɪt/}}v. 合作；配合}}{{The two companies agreed to cooperate on the project.}}
{{cope}}{/kəʊp/}}v. 应对；处理}}{{She learned to cope with stress through meditation.}}
{{core}}{/kɔːr/}}n. 核心；果心；adj. 核心的}}{{Innovation is the core of our business strategy.}}
{{corner}}{/ˈkɔːrnər/}}n. 角落；拐角}}{{The bank is located on the corner of the street.}}
{{corporate}}{/ˈkɔːrpərət/}}adj. 公司的；法人的}}{{The corporate culture emphasizes teamwork and innovation.}}
{{correct}}{/kəˈrekt/}}adj. 正确的；v. 改正}}{{Your answer is correct. Well done!}}
{{correspond}}{/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd/}}v. 通信；相当于；符合}}{{The results correspond with our expectations.}}
{{cost}}{/kɒst/}}n. 费用；v. 花费}}{{The cost of living has increased significantly.}}
{{council}}{/ˈkaʊnsl/}}n. 委员会；理事会}}{{The city council approved the new park project.}}
{{count}}{/kaʊnt/}}v. 计数；有价值}}{{Every vote counts in a democratic election.}}
{{country}}{/ˈkʌntri/}}n. 国家；乡村}}{{She traveled to many different countries last year.}}
